{"id": "tea:yatindramatadipika:1-3", "source": "src:yatindramatadipika", "location": {"ref": "1-3"}, "paraphrase": "There are three means of valid knowledge — perception, inference and scripture; comparison and the rest are included in these; all valid cognition is of the real.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:pramana", "trm:satkhyati"], "concepts": ["cpt:pramana", "cpt:satkhyati"], "teachers": ["tch:srinivasadasa"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U14-visistadvaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U14-visistadvaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yatindramatadipika:8", "source": "src:yatindramatadipika", "location": {"ref": "8"}, "paraphrase": "Souls are bound, freed or eternal; bound souls seek enjoyment or liberation; seekers of liberation seek either isolation of the self (kaivalya) or the Lord; seekers of the Lord are devotees (bhakta) or the surrendered (prapanna).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:classes-of-souls"], "terms": ["trm:mumuksu", "trm:prapanna"], "notes": "Chapter (avatāra) number recalled with low confidence.", "teachers": ["tch:srinivasadasa"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U14-visistadvaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U14-visistadvaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yatindramatadipika:9", "source": "src:yatindramatadipika", "location": {"ref": "9"}, "paraphrase": "The Lord has five forms: the supreme (para) in Vaikuṇṭha; the four vyūhas (Vāsudeva, Saṅkarṣaṇa, Pradyumna, Aniruddha), each manifesting pairs of the six qualities for creation, maintenance, dissolution and for meditation; the descents; the inner controller; and the image (arcā).", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-forms-of-god-pancaratra", "cpt:four-vyuhas"], "terms": ["trm:para-vasudeva", "trm:vyuha", "trm:vibhava", "trm:antaryamin", "trm:arca"], "notes": "Chapter number recalled with low confidence.", "teachers": ["tch:srinivasadasa"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U14-visistadvaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U14-visistadvaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yatindramatadipika:dravya", "source": "src:yatindramatadipika", "location": {"ref": "4-10 (the categories)"}, "paraphrase": "Reality is substance (dravya) or non-substance (adravya). The six substances are prakṛti, time, pure sattva (the eternal realm), attributive consciousness, the soul and the Lord; the ten non-substances are the three guṇas (sattva, rajas, tamas), the five sense qualities (sound, touch, form, taste, smell), conjunction and potency (śakti).", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:dravya-adravya", "cpt:three-kinds-of-acit"], "teachers": ["tch:srinivasadasa"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U14-visistadvaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U14-visistadvaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
